      "Contains a Kui invocation , with translation .",
      "Kui is not a literary language and does not possess a character of its own .",
      "In the Khondmals it has a broader sound , probably that of a in ‘ all , ’ and it is often written o in the specimens .",
      "In Kalahandi , the double ss in such words is replaced by ch ; thus , māchē , I am .",
      "D. is often pronounced as r . in the Khondmals ; thus , gōḍā and gōṛā , horse .",
      "In Kalahandi l is also often substituted for r ; thus , nēgāli , Standard nēgāri , a good woman .",
      "In the Khondmals we even find ēbāñju , he ; ēbāru , they , corresponding to Standard ēañju , ēāru .",
      "The Standard form is also used in Kalahandi .",
      "The substitution of ñj for n in connected languages is especially common in Kalahandi where we find forms such as ēāñji , Standard ēāni , his ."
    ]
